Z||000014||frontal lobe||08-08-2001||10:50 PM||||Hey b lo O,<P>Talk about torque steer!  I had a Mazda 626 turbo (had the same engine as the old Ford Probe GT) with 190 ft-lbs of torque.  5-speed.  Very excellent stealth sedan.  Looked just like the regular 4-door.  But, whoa, when you got on it, it was grab the steering wheel and hold on for the ride!<P>Finally I got old enough to have a little extra money to get a car with a nice v6, and couldn't find one with a manual transmission.  Only one about 3 years ago was the Maxima.  Then there was the Lincoln LS.  I'm glad to hear they are coming out with more of them now.  Can't wait.  I'm too young still to drive an automatic.<P>Now if they will only come out with a manual transmission minivan--hey, I've got kids, give me some slack here.||||reg||1
